/*  Objects — `Define object`, `a new …`, `'s` and `the … of`: `Pass1Hoist`'s object loop,
    `Pass2ResolveTypes`, `CheckObjectDefinition`, `CheckMethodBodyCore`, `InferObjectLiteral`,
    `InferPossessiveAccess`, `InferRecordNamedAccess` and `CheckObjectNamedSet` in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.*.cs`.

    ★ An object TYPE is its name: `(ObjectType "leaf" [])`, the node the parser writes for an
    annotation. What the type holds is read off its DEFINITION, which the checker keeps by name —
    the winning one, since a later definition of a name replaces an earlier.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    // ── What this checker can judge in an object ──────────────────────────

    Bind text to object-beyond-reach, given (the node statement):
        For each place in a series with (13), repeat:
            Define held as cast field-of on (statement, place).
            If held's kind is "list" and the number of held's children is greater than 0:
                Return "an object with {cast object-part-name on (place)}".
            Done.
        Done.
        For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            Define inner as cast bind-beyond-reach on (method).
            If inner is not "", return inner.
        Done.
        For each place in a series with (5, 6), repeat:
            For each declaration in (cast field-of on (statement, place))'s children, repeat:
                Define inner as cast property-beyond-reach on (declaration).
                If inner is not "", return inner.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each positional in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
            If cast beyond-types on (positional), return "an object with a {positional's kind} field".
        Done.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define held as cast field-of on (pair, 2).
            If cast beyond-types on (held), return "an object with a {held's kind} field".
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// A method bound `unto` a type, standing at the top level or in a pull.
    Bind text to unto-beyond-reach, given (the node statement):
        Define reach as cast bind-beyond-reach on (statement).
        If reach is not "a method bound 'unto' a type", return reach.
        // Its own checks, without the `unto` itself.
        If the number of statement's children is greater than 8, return "a Bind with {(cast field-of on (statement, 9))'s word}".
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (returned) or returned's kind is "AxiomType":
                Return "a function giving back a {returned's kind}".
            Done.
        Done.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast field-of on (parameter, 1).
            If cast beyond-types on (taken) or taken's kind is "AxiomType":
                Return "a function taking a {taken's kind}".
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast beyond-reach on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
    Done.

    Bind text to object-part-name, given (the number place):
        If place is 5, return "getters".
        If place is 6, return "setters".
        If place is 8, return "interfaces".
        If place is 12, return "blanks".
        If place is 13, return "types it carries".
        Return "defaults".
    Done.

    // ── Its definition ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to def-name, given (the node definition):
        Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (definition, 1)).
    Done.

    Bind text to embedded-name, given (the node definition):
        Define held as cast field-of on (definition, 7).
        If cast is-nothing on (held), return "".
        Return cast unquoted on (held).
    Done.

    Bind node to object-type-named, given (the text name):
        Return cast made on ("ObjectType", a series with (cast quoted on (name), cast listed)).
    Done.

    /// The definition behind an object type, or void.
    Bind voidable node to definition-of unto checker, given (the text name):
        Return the entry for name in one's defs.
    Done.

    /// Every positional field's type: its own, then the embedded object's, all the way down.
    Bind void to gather-positionals unto checker, given (the text name, the series of node into-list):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return.
        For each positional in (cast field-of on (definition, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Insert positional into into-list.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is not "", cast one's gather-positionals on (embedded, into-list).
    Done.

    /// Every named field, as `[name type]` pairs: its own, then the embedded object's.
    Bind void to gather-fields unto checker, given (the text name, the series of node into-list):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Insert pair into into-list.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is not "", cast one's gather-fields on (embedded, into-list).
    Done.

    /// A named field's type — its own, the embed handle, or promoted — or void.
    Bind voidable node to field-type-of unto checker, given (the text name, the text field):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return void.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) is field, return cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)).
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "" or cast one's definition-of on (embedded) is void, return void.
        If field is embedded, return cast object-type-named on (embedded).
        Return cast one's field-type-of on (embedded, field).
    Done.

    /// Is `field` the handle of an embedded object — reached by its type's name, not declared?
    Bind fact to is-embed-handle unto checker, given (the text name, the text field):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return false.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) is field, return false.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "" or cast one's definition-of on (embedded) is void, return false.
        Return field is embedded or cast one's is-embed-handle on (embedded, field).
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-permanent-field unto checker, given (the text name, the text field):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return false.
        For each written in (cast field-of on (definition, 11))'s children, repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (written) is field, return true.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "" or cast one's definition-of on (embedded) is void, return false.
        Return cast one's is-permanent-field on (embedded, field).
    Done.

    /// A method's type, its own or promoted — or void.
    Bind voidable node to method-type-of unto checker, given (the text name, the text method-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return void.
        For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) is method-name and cast one's is-nested-template on (method) is false:
                Return cast function-type-of on (method).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define filled-method as cast one's filled-method-of on (name, method-name).
        If filled-method is not void, return cast function-type-of on (filled-method).
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "", return void.
        Return cast one's method-type-of on (embedded, method-name).
    Done.

    /// A method of this object that leaves blanks — reached, it is filled per call.
    Bind fact to is-template-method unto checker, given (the text name, the text method-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return false.
        For each method in (cast field-of on (definition, 4))'s children, repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) is method-name and cast one's has-blanks on (method), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// A method written inside its definition that leaves blanks — one bound `unto` never does.
    Bind fact to is-nested-template unto checker, given (the node method):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (method, 5)) is false, return false.
        Return cast one's has-blanks on (method).
    Done.

    /// Does a type name one a book introduces — `matrix`, `chase` — anywhere inside it?
    Bind fact to mentions-book-type, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType", return cast book-introducing on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1))) is not "".
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom" and cast mentions-book-type on (inner), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Every method an object has: its own, then those bound `unto` it, in the order written.
    Bind series of node to all-methods unto checker, given (the node definition):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each method in (cast field-of on (definition, 4))'s children, repeat:
            Insert method into found.
        Done.
        Define attached as the entry for cast def-name on (definition) in one's untos.
        If attached is not void:
            For each method in attached's children, repeat:
                Insert method into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// Every name in a list of `[name …]` pairs, each in quotes, joined with commas.
    Bind text to quoted-names, given (the series of text names, the text suffix):
        Define out as a chase.
        Define first-one as true.
        For each name in names, repeat:
            If first-one is false, insert ", " into out.
            The first-one becomes false.
            Insert "'{name}'{suffix}" into out.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    Bind series of text to field-names unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define pairs as a series of node.
        Cast one's gather-fields on (name, pairs).
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each pair in pairs, repeat:
            Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) into names.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    Bind series of text to own-method-names unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define names as a series of text.
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return names.
        For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
            If cast one's is-nested-template on (method) is false, insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) into names.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    // ── Gathering them first ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Every object type, registered before anything is checked. A name that belongs to a book
    /// the language ships is refused; a second definition of any other name replaces the first.
    Bind void or failure to hoist-objects unto checker, given (the node program):
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            // A method is filed under its type's name; a getter under `get <type>`, a setter under `set <type>`.
            Define unto-place as 0.
            Define unto-row as 0.
            Define unto-key-lead as "".
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement":
                The unto-place becomes 5.
                The unto-row becomes cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
            Done.
            Otherwise if statement's kind is "GetterDeclaration":
                The unto-place becomes 4.
                The unto-row becomes cast getter-row on (statement).
                The unto-key-lead becomes "get ".
            Done.
            Otherwise if statement's kind is "SetterDeclaration":
                The unto-place becomes 5.
                The unto-row becomes cast setter-row on (statement).
                The unto-key-lead becomes "set ".
            Done.
            If unto-place is greater than 0:
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, unto-place)) is false:
                    Define target as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, unto-place)).
                    If cast is-bundled-module on (target) or (target in lowercase) is "rabbit":
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{target}' comes with the language, so 'unto' can't add members to it", "",
                            unto-row, "attach a member unto '{target}'",
                            "Define your own module object and pull it alongside the book instead.")).
                    Done.
                    Define filed-under as "{unto-key-lead}{target}".
                    Define attached as the entry for filed-under in one's untos.
                    If attached is void:
                        Define fresh-list as cast listed.
                        In one's untos, the entry for filed-under becomes fresh-list.
                        Insert filed-under into one's unto-order.
                        Cast fresh-list's add on (statement).
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Cast attached's add on (statement).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define claimed as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                Define name as cast def-name on (statement).
                If cast is-bundled-module on (name) or (name in lowercase) is "rabbit":
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' comes with the language, so its name can't be used for a new object", "",
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 9)), "define an object named '{name}'",
                        "Pick another name — 'Pull {name}.' always finds the one the language ships.")).
                Done.
                For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                    Cast check-buries-say-what on (method, "method") or pass the failure off.
                Done.
                // A definition that leaves a blank is a template: not a type, filled per use.
                Define is-template as the number of (cast field-of on (statement, 12))'s children is greater than 0.
                If is-template is false:
                    If (the entry for name in one's defs) is void, insert name into one's def-order.
                    In one's defs, the entry for name becomes statement.
                Done.
                // Its `unto` members join it, and a name it already has is refused.
                Define attached as the entry for name in one's untos.
                If attached is not void or (the entry for "get {name}" in one's untos) is not void or (the entry for "set {name}" in one's untos) is not void:
                    If (the entry for name in claimed) is not void:
                        Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'unto' members on a type defined twice")).
                    Done.
                    In claimed, the entry for name becomes true.
                Done.
                If attached is not void:
                    Define taken as a map from text to fact.
                    For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                        In taken, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) becomes true.
                    Done.
                    For each method in attached's children, repeat:
                        Define method-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)).
                        If (the entry for method-name in taken) is not void:
                            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' already has a method '{method-name}'", "",
                                cast numeric on (cast field-of on (method, 7)), "declare another method named '{method-name}' for '{name}'",
                                "Method names must be unique per type, whether declared nested or with 'unto'. Rename one of them.")).
                        Done.
                        In taken, the entry for method-name becomes true.
                        Cast check-buries-say-what on (method, "method") or pass the failure off.
                    Done.
                Done.
                Cast one's check-unto-property-names on (statement, "get ", 5, "getter", "Getter names must be unique per type. Rename one of them.") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's check-unto-property-names on (statement, "set ", 6, "setter", "Setter names must be unique per type. Rename one of them.") or pass the failure off.
                If is-template, in one's generic-defs, the entry for name becomes cast one's merged-template on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Whether every type name inside `shape` names something — `ResolveParamType`'s refusal, which
    /// alone of the checker's says no line: it is met while types are gathered, before any is.
    Bind void or failure to check-resolves unto checker, given (the node shape):
        Cast check-written-axiom on (shape) or pass the failure off.
        If shape's kind is "atom" or shape's kind is "list":
            For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
                Cast one's check-resolves on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
            If cast is-filled-type on (shape):
                Cast one's instantiate-object on (shape, 0) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            If (the entry for name in one's defs) is not void, return.
            If cast one's is-interface-name on (name), return.
            // A type a book introduces resolves to it inside the pull, and outside is left as the
            // name it is — C# refuses it later, where it is used, in its own words.
            If cast book-introducing on (name) is not "", return.
            If cast is-bundled-module on (name):
                Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a type named for a book")).
            Done.
            Return a failure "error\tThat doesn't work: '{name}' is not a defined type.\n\nDefine 'object {name}' before using it as a type name, or check the spelling.".
        Done.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            Cast one's check-resolves on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A getter's type — its own or promoted — or void. Read by field syntax, before a field.
    Bind voidable node to getter-type-of unto checker, given (the text name, the text getter-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return void.
        For each getter in cast one's all-getters on (definition), repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1)) is getter-name, return cast field-of on (getter, 2).
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "", return void.
        Return cast one's getter-type-of on (embedded, getter-name).
    Done.

    Bind series of text to own-getter-names unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define names as a series of text.
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
        If definition is void, return names.
        For each getter in cast one's all-getters on (definition), repeat:
            Insert cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1)) into names.
        Done.
        Return names.
    Done.

    /// Joined with commas, skipping the empty ones.
    Bind text to comma-joined, given (the series of text parts):
        Define out as a chase.
        Define first-one as true.
        For each part in parts, repeat:
            If part is not "":
                If first-one is false, insert ", " into out.
                The first-one becomes false.
                Insert part into out.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// `unto` methods whose type never turned up: an interface, or nothing at all.
    Bind void or failure to check-leftover-untos unto checker:
        For each target in one's unto-order, repeat:
            If (target starts with "get ") is false and (target starts with "set ") is false and (the entry for target in one's defs) is void
                    and cast one's is-absorbed on (target) is false:
                Define attached as the entry for target in one's untos but void is cast listed.
                Define first as item 1 of attached's children.
                Define reason as "'{target}' is not a defined object type".
                If cast one's is-interface-name on (target):
                    The reason becomes "'{target}' is an interface, not an object type — methods can't be attached to it with 'unto'".
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (reason, "", cast numeric on (cast field-of on (first, 7)),
                    "declare a method unto '{target}'",
                    "'unto' only attaches methods to object types defined in this program. Define 'object {target}' first, or check the spelling.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        // Then getters, then setters — C#'s order — and for these an interface gets no words of its own.
        For each lead in a series with ("get ", "set "), repeat:
            Define kind-word as "getter".
            If lead is "set ", the kind-word becomes "setter".
            For each filed-under in one's unto-order, repeat:
                If filed-under starts with lead:
                    Define target as the characters from 5 to the end of filed-under.
                    If (the entry for target in one's defs) is void and cast one's is-absorbed on (target) is false:
                        Define attached as the entry for filed-under in one's untos but void is cast listed.
                        Define first as item 1 of attached's children.
                        Define first-row as cast getter-row on (first).
                        If lead is "set ", the first-row becomes cast setter-row on (first).
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{target}' is not a defined object type", "", first-row,
                            "declare a {kind-word} unto '{target}'",
                            "'unto' only attaches {kind-word}s to object types defined in this program. Define 'object {target}' first, or check the spelling.")).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `unto` getters (or setters) joining a type: none may share a name with one it already has.
    Bind void or failure to check-unto-property-names unto checker, given (the node definition, the text lead,
            the number place, the text kind-word, the text fix):
        Define name as cast def-name on (definition).
        Define attached as the entry for "{lead}{name}" in one's untos.
        If attached is void, return.
        Define taken as a map from text to fact.
        For each declaration in (cast field-of on (definition, place))'s children, repeat:
            In taken, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        For each declaration in attached's children, repeat:
            Define declared-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (declaration, 1)).
            If (the entry for declared-name in taken) is not void:
                Define at-row as cast getter-row on (declaration).
                If lead is "set ", the at-row becomes cast setter-row on (declaration).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' already has a {kind-word} '{declared-name}'", "",
                    at-row, "declare another {kind-word} named '{declared-name}' for '{name}'", fix)).
            Done.
            In taken, the entry for declared-name becomes true.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A method that leaves blanks is a template, filled per call. Asked once every object type is
    /// registered, as C# asks it, so a type defined further down is not mistaken for a blank.
    Bind void or failure to check-method-blanks unto checker:
        For each name in one's def-order, repeat:
            Define definition as the entry for name in one's defs but void is cast listed.
            For each method in (cast field-of on (definition, 4))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's has-blanks on (method):
                    In one's generic-methods, the entry for "{name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}" becomes method.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `Pass2ResolveTypes`: every object's fields and methods, then every hoisted function.
    Bind void or failure to resolve-types unto checker:
        For each name in one's def-order, repeat:
            If (the entry for name in one's bundled) is not void, skip.
            Define definition as the entry for name in one's defs but void is cast listed.
            Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (definition, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
                If cast one's is-nested-template on (method) is false:
                    Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (method, 3)) or pass the failure off.
                    Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (method, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each getter in cast one's all-getters on (definition), repeat:
                Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (getter, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            For each setter in cast one's all-setters on (definition), repeat:
                Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (setter, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pair in item 1 of one's scopes, repeat:
            Define held as the value of pair.
            If held's shape's kind is "FunctionType":
                Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (held's shape, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (held's shape, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Checking a definition ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind void or failure to check-object-definition unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast def-name on (statement).
        // A superseded definition is dead: nothing reaches it, so nothing is checked in it.
        Define winner as the entry for name in one's defs.
        If winner is void, return.
        If cast shown-tree on (winner) is not cast shown-tree on (statement), return.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 9)).

        // A default is checked here, where it is written, not at each `a new` that leaves its field out.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 14))'s children, repeat:
            Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define declared as cast one's field-type-of on (name, field).
            If declared is not void:
                Define given-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                If cast is-none on (given-type) is false and cast assignable on (declared, given-type) is false:
                    If cast beyond-types on (given-type) or cast beyond-types on (declared):
                        Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {given-type's kind} default")).
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the default for '{field}' is a {cast type-words on (given-type)}, but the field holds a {cast type-words on (declared)}", "",
                        at-row, "give '{field}' a {cast type-words on (given-type)} default",
                        "Change the default to a {cast type-words on (declared)}, or change the field's type.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (statement).
        If embedded is not "":
            If cast one's definition-of on (embedded) is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("object '{name}' embeds '{embedded}', but no such object type is defined", "",
                    at-row, "embed '{embedded}' in '{name}'",
                    "Define object {embedded} with (...). before defining {name}.")).
            Done.
            Define promoted-fields as cast one's field-names on (embedded).
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
                For each other in promoted-fields, repeat:
                    If other is field:
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                            "'{name}' has its own field '{field}' which collides with a promoted field from '{embedded}'", "",
                            at-row, "define '{field}' in '{name}' while embedding '{embedded}'",
                            "Rename one of the fields. To access the embedded field explicitly, use 'the {field} of the {embedded} of ...'.")).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each method in cast one's all-methods on (statement), repeat:
                Define method-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)).
                If cast one's method-type-of on (embedded, method-name) is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                        "'{name}' has its own method '{method-name}' which collides with a promoted method from '{embedded}'", "",
                        at-row, "define '{method-name}' in '{name}' while embedding '{embedded}'",
                        "Rename one of the methods. To call the embedded method explicitly, use 'Cast {method-name} on the {embedded} of ...'.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        Cast one's check-conformance on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-property-names on (statement) or pass the failure off.

        // A module's bodies may leave another module to their caller — recorded as they are checked.
        Define earlier-module as one's checking-module.
        The one's checking-module becomes "".
        If cast is-module-definition on (statement), the one's checking-module becomes name.
        // A method that left a blank is checked per filling, never as itself.
        For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            If cast one's is-nested-template on (method) is false:
                Cast one's check-method-body on (method, name, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each getter in (cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's check-getter-body on (getter, name, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        For each setter in (cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's check-setter-body on (setter, name, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        The one's checking-module becomes earlier-module.
    Done.

    /// A method's body: `one` is the object, and otherwise it sees what a top-level function sees.
    Bind void or failure to check-method-body unto checker, given (the node method, the text owner,
            the number owner-row):
        Define filled-origin as the entry for "{owner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}" in one's origins.
        If filled-origin is not void:
            Try to:
                Cast one's check-method-core on (method, owner, owner-row).
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                Return a failure (cast filled-body-refused on (filled-origin, the message of the failure)).
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-method-core on (method, owner, owner-row) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-method-core unto checker, given (the node method, the text owner,
            the number owner-row):
        Define method-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)).
        Define returned as cast field-of on (method, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (method, 7)).
        Define buries as cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (method, 4)).
        Define earlier-recording as one's recording-stash.
        The one's recording-stash becomes "".
        If buries, the one's recording-stash becomes "{owner}'s {method-name}".
        Cast one's check-member-body on (owner, owner-row, cast field-of on (method, 3), at-row, true, returned,
            cast field-of on (method, 4)) or pass the failure off.
        The one's recording-stash becomes earlier-recording.
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false and cast is-void-or-failure on (returned) is false and buries is false
                and cast definitely-returns on (cast field-of on (method, 4)) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "method '{method-name}' is declared to give back a {cast type-words on (returned)}, but it can reach its end without returning one", "",
                at-row, "define a method that might not return a value",
                "Make sure every path through the method ends with a return statement.")).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The body of a method, a getter or a setter: `one` is the object, the parameters are bound,
    /// and otherwise it sees what a top-level function sees — functions and `permanently`
    /// constants. `parameters` is a list of `[<type> <name>]`; `resolving` says whether each type is
    /// checked to name something, which a method's are and a setter's is not.
    Bind void or failure to check-member-body unto checker, given (the text owner, the number owner-row,
            the node parameters, the number at-row, the fact resolving, the node returned, the node body):
        Define saved as one's scopes.
        Define saved-types as the number of one's type-scopes.
        Define fresh as cast builtin-scope.
        Cast carry-modules on (saved, fresh).
        Define earlier-hidden as one's hidden.
        Define hiding as a map from text to fact.
        For each scope in saved, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as the value of pair.
                If held's shape's kind is "FunctionType" or held's permanent:
                    In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    In hiding, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        The one's hidden becomes hiding.
        The one's scopes becomes a series with (fresh).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Cast one's bind-name on ("one", a new binding {
            the shape cast object-type-named on (owner),
            the established-by cast named-reference on ("one"), the line owner-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter true }).
        For each parameter in parameters's children, repeat:
            Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            If resolving, cast one's check-resolves on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's bind-name on (parameter-name, a new binding {
                the shape cast field-of on (parameter, 1),
                the established-by cast named-reference on (parameter-name), the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter true }).
        Done.

        Define earlier-in-function as one's in-function.
        Define earlier-line as one's function-line.
        Define earlier-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes 0.
        Increment one's nesting by 1.
        The one's in-function becomes true.
        If cast is-nothing on (returned), insert cast unknown-type into one's expected-returns.
        Otherwise, insert returned into one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes at-row.

        Cast one's check-block on (body) or pass the failure off.

        The one's in-function becomes earlier-in-function.
        Remove item (the number of one's expected-returns) from one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes earlier-line.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes earlier-depth.
        Decrement one's nesting by 1.
        The one's hidden becomes earlier-hidden.
        The one's scopes becomes saved.
        Cast one's trim-type-scopes on (saved-types).
    Done.

    // ── Making one ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `DefaultsFor`: the defaults a type's literal may lean on, down its embed chain — the nearer one wins.
    Bind series of node to defaults-for unto checker, given (the text name):
        Define found as a series of node.
        Define taken as a map from text to fact.
        Define current as name.
        While current is not "", repeat:
            Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (current).
            If definition is void, return found.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (definition, 14))'s children, repeat:
                Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
                If (the entry for field in taken) is void:
                    In taken, the entry for field becomes true.
                    Insert pair into found.
                Done.
            Done.
            The current becomes cast embedded-name on (definition).
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to infer-object-literal unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        Define positional-values as (cast field-of on (said, 2))'s children.
        Define named-values as (cast field-of on (said, 3))'s children.
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 4)).
        If cast is-bundled-module on (name) or (name in lowercase) is "rabbit":
            Define settled as "".
            Define fix as "Write 'Pull a book on {name}.' and use it inside that block.".
            If (name in lowercase) is "rabbit":
                The settled becomes "Pulling a rabbit is what opens its region, so one built this way would stand on no ground".
                The fix becomes "Write 'Pull a {name}.' (or 'Pull a {name} as <name>.') and use it inside that block.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' comes with the language — 'Pull' is how you get one", settled,
                at-row, "construct '{name}' with 'a new'", fix)).
        Done.
        // The name written is the template's, and every message says it; the filling is what is looked up.
        Define looked-up as name.
        If the number of (cast field-of on (said, 6))'s children is greater than 0:
            The looked-up becomes cast one's instantiate-object on (cast made on ("ObjectType",
                a series with (cast field-of on (said, 1), cast field-of on (said, 6))), at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast one's definition-of on (looked-up) is void:
            Define template as the entry for name in one's generic-defs.
            If template is not void, return a failure (cast unfilled-template-refusal on (name, template, at-row)).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is not a defined object type", "",
                at-row, "create a new {name} object", "Define the object type first: Define object {name} with (...).")).
        Done.
        If cast conforms-as on (cast one's definition-of on (looked-up) but void is cast listed, "book"):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a book, and a book is pulled, not made",
                "'{name}' says 'and book', so it owns no lifetime of its own — it is consulted rather than held",
                at-row, "construct '{name}' with 'a new'",
                "Write 'Pull a book on {name}.' and use its members inside that block.")).
        Done.

        Define positionals as a series of node.
        Cast one's gather-positionals on (looked-up, positionals).
        If the number of positional-values is not the number of positionals:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                "'{name}' expects {the number of positionals} positional field(s) (including promoted), but you provided {the number of positional-values}", "",
                at-row, "provide {the number of positional-values} positional field(s)",
                "'{name}' requires exactly {the number of positionals} positional field(s).")).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each value in positional-values, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define wanted as item place of positionals.
            Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, value-type) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} in a field")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("positional field {place} of '{name}' must be a {cast type-words on (wanted)}", "",
                    at-row, "provide a {cast type-words on (value-type)} for positional field {place}",
                    "Change the value to a {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
            Done.
        Done.

        Define all-fields as cast one's field-names on (looked-up).
        Define defaults as cast one's defaults-for on (looked-up).
        Define filled as a series of node.
        For each required in all-fields, repeat:
            Define present as false.
            For each pair in named-values, repeat:
                If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) is required, the present becomes true.
            Done.
            If present is false:
                For each pair in defaults, repeat:
                    If present is false and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) is required:
                        Insert pair into filled.
                        The present becomes true.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If present is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("field '{required}' of '{name}' is missing", "",
                    at-row, "create a {name} without field '{required}'",
                    "Add 'the {required} <value>' to the object literal, or give the field a default where '{name}' is defined: 'the ... {required} with default <value>'.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pair in filled, repeat:
            Cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        For each pair in named-values, repeat:
            Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
            Define wanted as cast one's field-type-of on (looked-up, field).
            If wanted is void:
                Define listing as "'{name}' has no named fields.".
                If the number of all-fields is greater than 0:
                    The listing becomes "Available named fields: {cast quoted-names on (all-fields, "")}.".
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' has no field named '{field}'", "",
                    at-row, "set unknown field '{field}'", listing)).
            Done.
            Define value-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (pair, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, value-type) is false:
                If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} in a field")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("field '{field}' of '{name}' must be a {cast type-words on (wanted)}", "",
                    at-row, "provide a {cast type-words on (value-type)} for field '{field}'",
                    "Change the value to a {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast object-type-named on (looked-up).
    Done.

    // ── Reaching into one ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `x's member` — a field, or a method when it is being called here.
    Bind node or failure to infer-possessive unto checker, given (the node said, the fact called-here):
        Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (target), return target.
        If target's kind is "BookType":
            Return cast one's infer-book-member on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)), member, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If target's kind is "InterfaceType":
            Define interface-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
            If (the entry for interface-name in one's interfaces) is void, return cast unknown-type.
            Define reached-method as cast one's interface-method-named on (interface-name, member).
            If reached-method is not void, return reached-method.
            Define offered as cast one's interface-method-names on (interface-name).
            Define fix as "Interface '{interface-name}' declares no methods.".
            If the number of offered is greater than 0, the fix becomes "Available methods: {cast quoted-names on (offered, "")}.".
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("interface '{interface-name}' has no method named '{member}'", "",
                at-row, "use 's to access '{member}' through interface '{interface-name}'", fix)).
        Done.
        If target's kind is not "ObjectType":
            If cast beyond-types on (target), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'s on a {target's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("possessive access ('s) requires an object, but got a {cast type-words on (target)}", "",
                at-row, "use 's on a {cast type-words on (target)}", "Only objects and books support the possessive 's syntax.")).
        Done.
        Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
        If cast one's definition-of on (owner) is void, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'s on a '{owner}'")).
        Cast one's check-hands-out on (owner, member, cast field-of on (said, 1), at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define method as cast one's method-type-of on (owner, member).
        If method is not void:
            If cast mentions-book-type on (method), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a method on a book's own types")).
        Done.
        If method is not void:
            If called-here is false:
                Define spoken as "{cast expression-words on (cast field-of on (said, 1))}'s {member}".
                Define fix as "Call it with 'cast': 'cast {spoken}'.".
                If the number of (cast field-of on (method, 1))'s children is greater than 0, the fix becomes "Call it with 'cast': 'cast {spoken}' on (…).".
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{member}' is a method of '{owner}', and a method is used by calling it", "",
                    at-row, "use '{spoken}' without calling it", fix)).
            Done.
            Return method.
        Done.
        Define getter as cast one's getter-type-of on (owner, member).
        If getter is not void, return getter.
        Define field as cast one's field-type-of on (owner, member).
        If field is not void, return field.

        Define available as cast comma-joined on (a series with (
            cast quoted-names on (cast one's field-names on (owner), ""),
            cast quoted-names on (cast one's own-getter-names on (owner), " (getter)"),
            cast quoted-names on (cast one's own-method-names on (owner), " (method)"))).
        Define fix as "'{owner}' has no fields, getters, or methods.".
        If available is not "", the fix becomes "Available: {available}.".
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{owner}' has no field, getter, or method named '{member}'", "",
            at-row, "access '{member}' on a {owner}", fix)).
    Done.

    /// `the <field> of <value>` — an object's field, a text's length, a map's size, a bits' width.
    Bind node or failure to infer-named-access unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        Define reached as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define target as cast one's infer on (reached) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (target), return target.
        Define kind as target's kind.
        Judge kind, where it is:
            It is "ObjectType":
                Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
                If cast one's definition-of on (owner) is void, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("the fields of a '{owner}'")).
                Define getter as cast one's getter-type-of on (owner, field).
                If getter is not void, return getter.
                Define found as cast one's field-type-of on (owner, field).
                If found is not void, return found.
                Define available as cast comma-joined on (a series with (
                    cast quoted-names on (cast one's field-names on (owner), ""),
                    cast quoted-names on (cast one's own-getter-names on (owner), " (getter)"))).
                Define fix as "'{owner}' has no named fields or getters.".
                If available is not "", the fix becomes "Available: {available}.".
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{owner}' has no field or getter named '{field}'", "",
                    at-row, "access field '{field}'", fix)).
            Done.
            It is "MappingType":
                If field is "key", return cast field-of on (target, 1).
                If field is "value", return cast field-of on (target, 2).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a mapping only has 'key' and 'value' fields", "",
                    at-row, "access field '{field}' on a mapping", "Use 'the key of mapping' or 'the value of mapping'.")).
            Done.
            It is "ExceptionMarkerType":
                If field is "message", return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("an exception only has a 'message' field", "",
                    at-row, "access field '{field}' on an exception", "Use 'the message of the exception'.")).
            Done.
            It is "FailureMarkerType":
                If field is "message", return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
                If field is "category", return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a failure only has 'message' and 'category' fields", "",
                    at-row, "access field '{field}' on a failure",
                    "Use 'the message of the failure' or 'the category of the failure'.")).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                // ⚠ Before the map's `size`: a set is stored as a map and reads like a collection.
                If kind is "SetType" and field is "size":
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the size of' works on maps, and this is a set", "",
                        at-row, "get the size of {cast expression-words on (reached)}",
                        "Write 'the number of {cast expression-words on (reached)}' instead.")).
                Done.
                // `rows` and `columns` are counts on a matrix, and ordinary field names everywhere else.
                If kind is "MatrixType":
                    If field is "rows" or field is "columns", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a matrix only has 'rows' and 'columns'", "",
                        at-row, "access field '{field}' on a matrix",
                        "Use 'the rows of m' or 'the columns of m'. For an element, use 'the item at (row, column) of m'.")).
                Done.
                If cast beyond-types on (target):
                    Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("the {field} of a {kind}")).
                Done.
                If kind is "RecordType", return cast record-field-access on (target, field, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                If kind is "BitsType" and field is "width", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
                If kind is "TextType" and field is "length", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
                If kind is "MapType" and field is "size", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
                If field is "length":
                    Define fix as "Only text values have a character length. For series, use 'the number of series'.".
                    Define union-fix as cast narrowing-fix on (reached, target, "TextType").
                    If union-fix is not "", the fix becomes union-fix.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the length of' works on text only", "",
                        at-row, "get the length of a {cast type-words on (target)}", fix)).
                Done.
                If field is "size":
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'the size of' works on maps", "",
                        at-row, "get the size of a {cast type-words on (target)}",
                        "For series, use 'the number of'. For text, use 'the length of'.")).
                Done.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you're trying to access field '{field}' on something that isn't a record or object", "",
                    at-row, "access a named field of a {cast type-words on (target)}", "Only records and objects have named fields.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `item N of <object>` — its Nth positional field, own first and then the embedded object's.
    Bind node or failure to object-item unto checker, given (the node target, the node index-said,
            the number at-row, the text verb):
        Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
        If cast is-nothing on (index-said):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'last' doesn't work on objects", "", at-row,
                "use 'last' on an object", "Use a position like 'the first of ...' or a field name like 'the city of ...'.")).
        Done.
        If index-said's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return cast unknown-type.
        Define positionals as a series of node.
        Cast one's gather-positionals on (owner, positionals).
        Define spot as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (index-said, 1)).
        // C# truncates toward zero, as a cast to int does.
        Define whole as spot - (spot % 1).
        If whole is less than 1 or whole is greater than the number of positionals:
            Define said as "'{owner}' has {the number of positionals} positional field(s) — there is no position {whole}".
            Define fix as "Positions run 1 through {the number of positionals}.".
            If the number of positionals is 0:
                The said becomes "'{owner}' has no positional fields".
                The fix becomes "'{owner}' has no positional fields. Access fields by name instead.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (said, "", at-row, "{verb} {whole}", fix)).
        Done.
        Return item whole of positionals.
    Done.

    // ── Writing into one ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `x's field becomes …` and `the field of x becomes …`: the shared field write.
    Bind void or failure to check-field-write unto checker, given (the text owner, the text field,
            the node value, the number at-row, the number target-depth, the text region-action):
        If cast one's is-permanent-field on (owner, field):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{field}' is permanent — it is set when the {owner} is made, and never changes after", "",
                at-row, "change '{field}' after the {owner} was made",
                "Give '{field}' its value in the 'a new {owner}' literal. If it has to change later, declare the field without 'permanently'.")).
        Done.
        Define wanted as cast one's field-type-of on (owner, field).
        If wanted is void:
            Define names as cast one's field-names on (owner).
            Define fix as "Object '{owner}' has no named fields.".
            If the number of names is greater than 0:
                Define listing as a chase.
                Define first-one as true.
                For each name in names, repeat:
                    If first-one is false, insert ", " into listing.
                    The first-one becomes false.
                    Insert name into listing.
                Done.
                The fix becomes "Available named fields: {listing converted to text}.".
            Done.
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("object '{owner}' has no field named '{field}'", "",
                at-row, "set field '{field}'", fix)).
        Done.
        If cast one's is-embed-handle on (owner, field):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{field}' is an embedded object handle — you can't replace the whole embedded object", "",
                at-row, "set the embed handle '{field}'", "Mutate individual fields of the embedded object instead.")).
        Done.
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (value) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (value-type) is false and cast assignable on (wanted, value-type) is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (value-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("a {value-type's kind} in a field")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("field '{field}' holds a {cast type-words on (wanted)}, not a {cast type-words on (value-type)}", "",
                at-row, "set field '{field}' to a {cast type-words on (value-type)}",
                "Field '{field}' has type {cast type-words on (wanted)}.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-region-store on (value, value-type, target-depth, at-row, region-action) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-possessive-set unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (target), return.
        If target's kind is not "ObjectType":
            If cast beyond-types on (target), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'s on a {target's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("possessive assignment requires an object, but got a {cast type-words on (target)}", "",
                at-row, "set '{member}' on a {cast type-words on (target)}",
