        Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
        If cast one's definition-of on (owner) is void, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("'s on a '{owner}'")).
        If cast one's is-permanent-field on (owner, member):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{member}' is permanent — it is set when the {owner} is made, and never changes after", "",
                at-row, "change '{member}' after the {owner} was made",
                "Give '{member}' its value in the 'a new {owner}' literal. If it has to change later, declare the field without 'permanently'.")).
        Done.
        Define setter as cast one's setter-of on (owner, member).
        If setter is not void:
            Cast one's check-setter-write on (setter, member, cast field-of on (statement, 3), at-row,
                cast one's container-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)),
                "set '{member}' to a value from a shorter-lived region than the object") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-field-write on (owner, member, cast field-of on (statement, 3), at-row,
            cast one's container-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)),
            "set '{member}' to a value from a shorter-lived region than the object") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to check-named-set unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define field as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (target), return.
        If target's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define owner as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
            If cast one's definition-of on (owner) is void, return a failure (cast not-judged on ("the fields of a '{owner}'")).
            If cast one's is-permanent-field on (owner, field):
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{field}' is permanent — it is set when the {owner} is made, and never changes after", "",
                    at-row, "change '{field}' after the {owner} was made",
                    "Give '{field}' its value in the 'a new {owner}' literal. If it has to change later, declare the field without 'permanently'.")).
            Done.
            Define setter as cast one's setter-of on (owner, field).
            If setter is not void:
                Cast one's check-setter-write on (setter, field, cast field-of on (statement, 3), at-row,
                    cast one's container-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)),
                    "set field '{field}' to a value from a shorter-lived region") or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Cast one's check-field-write on (owner, field, cast field-of on (statement, 3), at-row,
                cast one's container-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)),
                "set field '{field}' to a value from a shorter-lived region") or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If target's kind is "RecordType":
            Cast one's check-record-set on (target, statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast beyond-types on (target):
            Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("setting the {field} of a {target's kind}")).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you're trying to set field '{field}' on something that isn't a record or object", "",
            at-row, "set a named field on a {cast type-words on (target)}", "Only records and objects have named fields.")).
    Done.
Done.
